# The key that signs Aperire One releases, in OpenSSH allowed_signers format.
#
# Every release publishes release.json and a detached signature over it,
# release.json.sig. The installer and the updater refuse a release whose
# signature does not verify against a key on this list. docs/RELEASE-SIGNING.md
# carries the same line and its fingerprint, and says how to check a release
# by hand.
#
# One plain ssh-ed25519 key. Two only during a key change, in the two signed
# steps the guide describes. Every line has this shape:
#
#   aperire-release-key namespaces="aperire-release" ssh-ed25519 <base64> [comment]
#
# This is the committed release key: a host whose set is not this one trusts
# a lab or test key.
aperire-release-key namespaces="aperire-release" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHIkP5Gqz/T/4taeWVb5repX47RKnpgYkNJPJ69Di9kp aperire-release-key-1
